WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.920
Since making its debut on the&nbsp;
History channel way back in 2010,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:08.640
American Pickers has become one of the most&nbsp;
beloved shows on television, airing over 300&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:13.680
episodes and counting. It's also made stars&nbsp;
of series regulars Frank Fritz and Mike Wolfe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.440
who've managed to turn their love of digging&nbsp;
for gold in the backyards and broken-down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:22.160
barns of America into a full-blown media&nbsp;
empire — one that's also afforded them a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:27.120
pair of cathedral-like antique stores, both&nbsp;
of which are now legit tourist destinations.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.960
But there's at least one antique they&nbsp;
found that American Pickers star Mike&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:34.640
Wolfe wishes he had held onto. And&nbsp;
it's not what you probably think.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:39.120
Wolfe, of course, is famous for his love of&nbsp;
bikes. Whether it's vintage motorcycles or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:44.160
rusted out old pedal pushers, Wolfe has a thing&nbsp;
for everything two wheeled. So you'd be forgiven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:49.280
for assuming that his biggest regret is getting&nbsp;
rid of an old Harley or Huffy. You'd be forgiven,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:53.280
but you'd still be wrong, because the&nbsp;
item Wolfe is most miffed about getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:57.520
rid of is actually an old pair of&nbsp;
vintage children's cowboy boots.

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:59.280
Sounds weird, but you know what they say.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:02.560
"If the boot. Fits."

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.200
"Okay, cowboy."

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:12.080
In a 2016 interview with Country Living, Wolfe&nbsp;
gave the whole sad backstory, while also advising&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:16.080
any would-be pickers to listen to that little&nbsp;
voice in the back of your head. When it tells&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:20.320
you to buy something, buy it, and when it&nbsp;
tells you not to sell something, don't sell it.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:24.240
In Wolfe's case, that pair of kid's cowboy&nbsp;
boots took on a whole new significance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:28.160
after his wife became pregnant with their&nbsp;
daughter Charlie. He told Country Living,

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:32.240
"Before Charlie was born, I always had&nbsp;
a thing for vintage kids' cowboy boots.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:36.320
I once found a pair, but I sold them&nbsp;
and immediately regretted doing so."

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:39.120
Luckily, Wolfe got a second&nbsp;
chance and he made the most of it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:41.680
turning an interest into a full blown obsession.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:46.240
"When Jodi was pregnant, I found a second pair.&nbsp;
It felt like fate, so I started collecting them."

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:50.240
Now, Wolfe buys vintage children's&nbsp;
cowboy boots every chance he gets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.400
and once he buys them, they stay with him;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:56.800
he showed off at least a half dozen pairs to&nbsp;
Country Living as proof of his dedication.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.480
Wolfe also shared some of his secrets&nbsp;
to amassing a collection like his,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:04.800
whether your interest is in kids' cowboy&nbsp;
boots, old bikes, or some other type of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:08.960
rusty gold. His first tip is simply to&nbsp;
follow your nose and see what you find.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:13.120
That run down barn over there? Who knows,&nbsp;
it might have a massive pile of tiny old&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:17.680
cowboy boots in it. Or maybe it will have&nbsp;
just one gigantic boot instead, who knows!

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:22.000
"Okay, stand it up. That's awesome!"

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:22.960
Wolfe explained,

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:25.760
"I've found my best picks by&nbsp;
driving to the middle of nowhere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:28.000
then taking the first gravel road I see."

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.760
Of course, there are some dangers in approaching&nbsp;
random houses in the middle of nowhere.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:36.640
"If someone's putting their boot on&nbsp;
your neck, you gotta get used to that."

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:42.000
And for prospective pickers hoping to spice&nbsp;
up their home with some vintage artifacts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.240
Wolfe had another big tip: don't stop&nbsp;
at just one, buy multiples if you can.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:50.080
"They can be really cool when done right.&nbsp;
I like to display objects with similar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:54.480
textures, time periods, and genres&nbsp;
for visual continuity. In my office,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:57.040
each shelf has a theme: bikes, motorcycles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:01.600
aviation, and cars. It's easy to go overboard,&nbsp;
though, so I like to stick to just one spot."

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:04.800
Like Mike Wolfe with his vintage&nbsp;
bikes and his wee little boots,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:08.080
once you find something you're passionate&nbsp;
about, the thrill of the hunt and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:12.720
excitement of finding a new addition to your&nbsp;
collection is what makes picking so much fun.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:16.960
Of course, while Wolfe no doubt will be&nbsp;
adding to his boot collection in the future,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:21.440
he and partner Frank Fritz were derailed&nbsp;
in 2020, as the Coronavirus forced them to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:26.000
temporarily shut down production of American&nbsp;
Pickers. Wolfe used that time to advocate for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.480
reinvesting in local communities, and to&nbsp;
focus on another part of his collection:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:34.640
buying and restoring vintage buildings to&nbsp;
help bring back small town Main Street.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:38.720
"these communities are an important&nbsp;
part of the heart and soul of america"

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.960
From boots to boutiques, turns&nbsp;
out that in the world of picking,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:44.960
there's nothing too big... or too small!

